# Input Validation Reviewer Rule v1.0 STRICT

**Do not inline-audit.** Invoke **`input_validation_reviewer`** -> `.cursor/agents/input_validation_reviewer.md`.

## References

| Artifact | Path |
|---|---|
| Policy | `.cursor/skills/input_validation_reviewer/POLICY.md` |
| Scan skill | `.cursor/skills/input_validation_reviewer/SKILL.md` |
| Report path | `AI/input_validation_reviewer/input_validation_reviewer_report.md` |
| Report line | `input_validation_reviewer v1.0 STRICT` |

**POLICY.md wins.**

## Invoke when

Use before deploy or when controllers, DTOs, forms, JSON APIs, imports, webhooks, headers, cookies, file metadata, regex validation, or frontend validation changes.

Skip for generated output, `target/`, `node_modules/`, and docs-only edits unless the docs define validation policy.

## Non-negotiable rule

Frontend validation is UX only. If a field is validated only by HTML, JavaScript, browser constraints, or UI behavior, the reviewer must report **IV03 - No frontend-only validation**.

Backend/server-side validation must independently reject direct invalid requests that bypass the UI.

## Finding table

Every finding includes:

| Row | Content |
|---|---|
| Evidence | Bad line or runtime proof from project |
| Policy Rule | POLICY.md - CHECK-ID - citation |
| Pattern | SKILL.md section 8 pattern |
| Mechanism | Plain English + framework/API names |
| Security property | What must be true after fix |
| Prohibited | Short label only |
| Verify | Action + pass signal |

Allowed verdicts: **PASS**, **FAIL**, **MANUAL_REVIEW**, **N/A**. `UNCLEAR` is forbidden.
